ex=news['examples'][0]
n+=section('Try the recorded model examples','<p>I ran three illustrative passages through the supplied model checkpoint. The viewer replays those outputs. The percentage is the classifier’s score for its “fake” class. It describes a model prediction, without verifying the story.</p>'+
 f'''<div class="example-box"><label for="example-select">Choose a passage</label><select id="example-select">{''.join(f'<option value="{i}">{escape(example["title"])}</option>' for i,example in enumerate(news["examples"]))}</select><div aria-live="polite"><blockquote id="example-text">{escape(ex['text'])}</blockquote><div class="prediction"><div><span>Model label</span><strong id="example-label">{ex['label'].title()}</strong></div><div><span>Score for “fake”</span><strong id="example-score">{ex['fake']*100:.2f}%</strong></div></div></div><p class="fine">The saved thresholds classify scores up to 44% as “real” and 66% or above as “fake”. Intermediate scores receive “uncertain”.</p></div>''','examples')
n+=section('Model and testing','<p>The Flask code combines two TF-IDF and Logistic Regression pipelines. One represents words and phrases, while the other represents character patterns. The app averages their predicted probabilities before applying the saved decision thresholds.</p><p>The checkpoint records 4,170 training examples and 1,390 held-out examples. Its thresholds were tuned using the holdout. The reported 88.42% accuracy describes this project evaluation.</p><p>I prepared functional and regression test cases for the web and extension workflows. Each defect report records the reproduction steps, expected behavior, actual behavior, and severity.</p>','testing')
n+=section('Project files','<p>Read the original Windows setup guide or inspect the actual classifier prediction method, input template, and extension source.</p>'+links_block([('Original setup guide (DOCX)','/documents/TruthLens_Setup_Guide.docx','doc',True),('Source excerpts (ZIP)','/documents/veritas-source-excerpts.zip','code',True),('Academic project overview (PDF)','/documents/VERITAS_Project_Portfolio.pdf','doc',True)]),'downloads')
(root/'work/veritas.html').write_text(layout('VERITAS News Classifier | Muhammad Danial','Original Python project interface, Chrome extension, saved classifier examples, source excerpts and testing approach.',paths['news'],nhead+article_body(n,sidebar([('interface','Original interface'),('examples','Model examples'),('testing','Model & testing'),('downloads','Project files')],'Software development · Final-year project'))+next_link(paths['caml'],'CAML-Net research')))
chead=case_head('Applied machine learning research','CAML-Net','What happens to a chest X-ray classifier when the accompanying radiology report is missing or mismatched? I explored that question with paired studies from Open-I.',['PyTorch','DenseNet-121','BioBERT','Cross-attention'],'Exploratory Open-I research prototype · Modal Tesla T4 · November 2026')
chead+='<div class="shell top-measures">'+kpis([('3,826','Paired Open-I studies'),('383','Held-out test studies'),('27','Recorded checkpoints')])+'</div>'
c=section('How the model works','<p>Each study supplies a chest image and a written radiology report. Frozen DenseNet-121 and BioBERT encoders extract visual and text features. Bidirectional cross-attention lets the two streams share information before predicting 14 report-derived observations.</p><ol class="method-list"><li><strong>Encode both inputs</strong><span>Map image regions and report tokens into 512-dimensional representations.</span></li><li><strong>Compare and combine</strong><span>Measure the discrepancy between shared features. Use conflict and uncertainty signals to adjust how much each input contributes.</span></li><li><strong>Evaluate each prediction</strong><span>Produce a probability and an uncertainty indicator for each observation. Estimate probability calibration on a separate split.</span></li></ol>','method')
pop=caml['population']['splits']
c+=section('Experiment design','<p>The final experiment used a Tesla T4 GPU, three training seeds (11, 22, 33), and nine configurations. The splits contained 2,676 training, 384 validation, 383 calibration, and 383 test studies. The run manifest records one checkpoint for each seed and configuration.</p><p>Fourteen observation targets include findings such as lung opacity and cardiomegaly, alongside “No Finding” and “Support Devices”. Of the 383 test studies, 376 had known weak targets for scoring. Unknown labels were masked.</p>','experiment')
mopts=[('macro_auroc','Macro AUROC'),('macro_average_precision','Macro average precision'),('micro_f1','Micro F1'),('brier','Brier score'),('pooled_ece_10_bins','Pooled ECE')]
mainmodels=caml['models'][:4]
def bars(items,metric):
    return ''.join(f'<div class="model-bar{" is-full" if r["key"]=="full" else ""}"><span>{models[r["key"]]}</span><div aria-hidden="true"><i style="width:{100*r[metric]:.3f}%"></i></div><strong>{r[metric]:.5f}</strong></div>' for r in items)
comparison_table=table(['Configuration','AUROC','Macro AP','Micro F1','Brier','ECE'],[[models[r['key']]]+[f'{r[k]:.5f}' for k,_ in mopts] for r in caml['models']],'Three-seed ensemble · all nine configurations')
c+=section('What the comparison showed','<p>Full CAML-Net reached a macro AUROC of <strong>0.93759</strong>. Image only scored 0.75185, and text only reached 0.95318. The reports carried a strong signal for these report-derived labels. Full fusion also recorded a lower pooled calibration error than either single-input model.</p>'+
 f'''<div class="metric-box"><label for="metric-select">Compare models by metric</label><select id="metric-select">{''.join(f'<option value="{v}">{n}</option>' for v,n in mopts)}</select><div class="model-bars" id="model-bars" aria-live="polite">{bars(mainmodels,'macro_auroc')}</div><p class="fine" id="metric-note">Higher is better. AUROC measures how well scores rank positive examples above negative ones.</p></div>
<details class="detail-table"><summary>All nine configurations, including ablations</summary>{comparison_table}</details><p class="fine">Scores are from the ensemble of three calibrated models. Micro F1 uses a 0.5 threshold. ECE uses ten pooled probability bins.</p>''','comparison')
maskrows=caml['missing']
maskopts=''.join(f'<option value="{row["missing"]}">{row["missing"]}% missing</option>' for row in maskrows)
mask_table=table(['Reports removed','Mean AUROC','Mean micro F1','Mean Brier'],[[f'{r["missing"]}%',f'{r["macro_auroc"]:.5f}',f'{r["micro_f1"]:.5f}',f'{r["brier"]:.5f}'] for r in maskrows],'Full-model results averaged over three masking draws')
c+=section('What changed when reports went missing','<p>I evaluated the full ensemble at five report-removal rates with fixed model weights. With 80% of reports missing, micro F1 fell from 0.82034 to 0.50368. Each point averages three masking draws.</p>'+
 f'''<figure class="full-research-chart">{model_art()}<figcaption>Full CAML-Net ensemble · Mean micro F1 over three masking draws at each removal rate.</figcaption></figure><div class="mask-box"><label for="missing-select">Share of reports removed</label><select id="missing-select">{maskopts}</select><dl class="kpis" aria-live="polite"><div><dt>Mean AUROC</dt><dd id="mask-auc">0.93759</dd></div><div><dt>Mean micro F1</dt><dd id="mask-f1">0.82034</dd></div><div><dt>Mean Brier score</dt><dd id="mask-brier">0.01622</dd></div></dl></div><details class="detail-table"><summary>All five report-removal rates</summary>{mask_table}</details>''','missing')
c+=section('Conflict, uncertainty, and limits','''<p>A controlled test swapped reports between 376 studies whose known labels differed. The model distinguished matched from swapped pairs with AUROC 0.67185. This tests sensitivity to an artificial mismatch. Clinical contradiction detection requires expert-reviewed cases.</p>
<p>The evaluation used 1,000 group-bootstrap draws and 2,000 paired permutations with Holm adjustment. The full model’s micro F1 interval was 0.78172–0.85667. Adjusted comparisons on Brier score, log loss, and micro F1 did not establish superiority over text only.</p>
<p>Open-I labels were mapped from the reports, some findings had only one or two positive test examples, and the test partition had been examined previously. Clinical validation and independent MIMIC-CXR evaluation remain open.</p>''','limits')
c+=section('Explore the research files','<p>The GPU review documents the recorded run and its limitations. The tables include all nine models, the missing-report experiments, statistical comparisons, and per-label support. The source archive contains the core implementation files matched to the recorded run.</p>'+links_block([('One-page results (PDF)','/documents/CAML_Net_Research_Portfolio.pdf','doc',True),('Full GPU review (PDF)','/documents/caml-gpu-review.pdf','doc',True),('Model comparison (CSV)','/documents/caml-model-comparison.csv','sheet',True),('Evaluation tables (ZIP)','/documents/caml-evaluation-tables.zip','plot',True),('Model source (ZIP)','/documents/caml-model-source.zip','code',True)]),'downloads')
(root/'work/caml-net.html').write_text(layout('CAML-Net Chest X-ray & Report Research | Muhammad Danial','Explore the actual Open-I GPU run, nine model configurations, missing-report experiments, aggregate data and source code.',paths['caml'],chead+article_body(c,sidebar([('method','Architecture'),('experiment','Experiment design'),('comparison','Model comparison'),('missing','Missing reports'),('limits','Statistical limits'),('downloads','Research files')],'Open-I / IU Chest X-ray · Research prototype'))+next_link(CASE_URL,'NTDC Excel master data')))
